# Chip Estimate Integrity — Phase B: Coverage check (CORE)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (locked before Phase B implementation edits)
# B1 GIVEN an assessment bedroom count and dwelling type, WHEN expected coverage
#    is built, THEN it contains bedroom × count + kitchen + living room + bathroom;
#    House additionally contains garage + basement, while Apartment/Condo/Townhome
#    contain neither. An absent assessment bedroom count contributes zero bedroom
#    expectations, preserving the existing refinement-input migration contract.
# B2 GIVEN scanned room labels, WHEN coverage is compared, THEN labels normalize
#    case-insensitively through the documented RESO-derived synonym map; unmatched
#    scanned rooms remain visible extras, and missing bedrooms render numbered
#    expected rows (Bedroom 2, Bedroom 3, and so on).
# B3 GIVEN an expected-but-unseen room, WHEN Add a clip is chosen, THEN capture is
#    prefilled for that room and a completed scan resolves it; WHEN Nothing there
#    is chosen, THEN its stable expected-room ID is saved as coverageConfirmed and
#    survives metadata encode/decode and Firestore read-back.
# B4 GIVEN N unresolved unseen rooms on a scan-derived scope, WHEN pricing runs,
#    THEN the low bound is unchanged and the high-side multiplier is multiplied by
#    (1 + 0.15 × N), capped at the bedrooms-fallback high-side multiplier for the
#    same access/packing scope. Unit tests prove the cap. Resolved rooms do not widen.
# B5 GIVEN unresolved unseen rooms, WHEN an estimate and comparison card render,
#    THEN they contain exactly "Some rooms weren't scanned."; when all expected
#    rooms are scanned or confirmed, neither widening nor disclosure occurs.
# B6 GIVEN the Phase B UI fixture, WHEN the room hub renders, THEN a screenshot shows
#    "Scanned:" and "Not seen:" plus both actions. CORE tests, simulator tests, a
#    fresh-context validator, and walked hub-file diffs pass. No deploy occurs.
